{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791790001,"nonce":"fR5+dS65Kmy9uBmbmdOBs7Xqzxc=","title":"Decisions scorer: spend lost when a row write fails after a billed request","message":"Same ordering bug as 6c33b40, left out of that fix to keep scope. In scoring/decisions.py (score_sync_decisions, around line 955), _record_spend runs inside the same _txn as the per-job _write calls, so if _write or map_job raises an unexpected error the whole transaction rolls back and the billed request's spend is not recorded, and the cap undercounts. Fix: record llm_spend for the request in its own committed _txn right after the response returns, then write rows in a second transaction, as done for screen.score_with, _score_sync_chunk and _score_sync_packed in 6c33b40. Test: monkeypatch decisions._write to raise and assert llm_spend has the call.","files":null}]}